00:32:41.460 --> 00:32:42.293
Yeah.

00:32:42.293 --> 00:32:43.870
So if you think about
the selection process.

00:32:43.870 --> 00:32:44.703
Pretty elite.

00:32:44.703 --> 00:32:47.143
Like when you meet somebody
who's and NBA player,

00:32:48.530 --> 00:32:49.890
I don't know what the percentages are

00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:51.730
of like the number of
people who want to be in

00:32:51.730 --> 00:32:53.390
the NBA and the number of people who are,

00:32:53.390 --> 00:32:55.720
but it's an elite thing,

00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:58.696
but it's somebody who's
really good at basketball.

00:32:58.696 --> 00:33:00.750
Which is impressive in and of itself.

00:33:00.750 --> 00:33:03.410
But it's still basketball, I mean like,

00:33:03.410 --> 00:33:06.470
there's no indications
that they're gonna be good

00:33:06.470 --> 00:33:08.290
at everything else.

00:33:08.290 --> 00:33:12.500
But an astronaut has gotten, you know,

00:33:12.500 --> 00:33:15.220
they have gone through this evaluation

00:33:15.220 --> 00:33:18.010
to test their physical capabilities,

00:33:18.010 --> 00:33:21.390
their mental capabilities,
their emotional stability,

00:33:21.390 --> 00:33:23.370
they have psych evals
because you're gonna go up

00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:24.930
and you're gonna be in this confined space

00:33:24.930 --> 00:33:27.590
and you can't go nuts.

00:33:27.590 --> 00:33:31.800
You can't be difficult, you
can't be hard to get along with.

00:33:31.800 --> 00:33:34.100
You can't not play well with others.

